IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`
IMPORT `wra3-pt4-s95`

-- wra3-pt4-s77-84.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 4, sections 77 to 84
-- (personal independence payment: the allowance, the two components, how ability and the required period are decided,
-- terminal illness, pensionable age, the EU rule). Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text
-- rendering of legislation.gov.uk (version 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST FALSE is the text's own "no"
-- ("is not entitled", "unless", "while", a failed "if" within the provision that holds it); NOTHING is "not covered"
-- (silent, points to regulations, limited by its own wording). A result named "is not barred" means only that THIS
-- provision's bar does not apply; it never means entitled or payable. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Values the regulations supply, and judgments the Act hands to the regulations' assessment (section 80), are inputs.

§ `s 77 Personal independence payment`

-- src:1347 | (1) An allowance known as personal independence payment is payable in accordance with this Part.
@ref s 77(1) (src:1347)
`s 77(1) the allowance known as personal independence payment` MEANS `personal independence payment`

-- (2) says what an entitlement to personal independence payment may be an entitlement to: the daily living component,
-- the mobility component, or both.
-- src:1348 | (2) A person's entitlement to personal independence payment may be an entitlement to—
-- src:1349 | (a) the daily living component (see section 78);
-- src:1350 | (b) the mobility component (see section 79); or
-- src:1351 | (c) both those components.
@ref s 77(2) (src:1348-1351)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to the daily living component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Component of personal independence payment`
`s 77(2) the components the person's entitlement is an entitlement to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is entitled to the daily living component` AND `the person is entitled to the mobility component`
        THEN LIST `daily living component`, `mobility component`                          -- (c) both those components
        IF `the person is entitled to the daily living component` THEN LIST `daily living component`   -- (a)
        IF `the person is entitled to the mobility component` THEN LIST `mobility component`           -- (b)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection lists what an entitlement may be; it does not say what a person entitled to neither has
        OTHERWISE EMPTY

-- src:1352 | (3) A person is not entitled to personal independence payment unless the person meets prescribed conditions relating to residence and presence in Great Britain.
@ref s 77(3) (src:1352)
GIVEN `the prescribed conditions relating to residence and presence in Great Britain are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(3) the person is not barred for want of the prescribed residence and presence conditions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the prescribed conditions relating to residence and presence in Great Britain are met`
    WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not entitled to personal independence payment unless the person meets prescribed conditions"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the conditions are left to regulations
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

-- src:1353 | (4) A person is not entitled to personal independence payment while they are entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance, pension age disability payment, adult disability payment or child disability payment.
@ref s 77(4) (src:1353)
GIVEN `the Scottish disability payments the person is entitled to` IS A LIST OF `s 95 Scottish disability assistance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(4) the person is not barred by being entitled to a Scottish disability payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Scottish disability payments the person is entitled to`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not entitled to personal independence payment while they are entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance, pension age disability payment, adult disability payment or child disability payment"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 78 Daily living component`

-- The caller's results from the other provisions of Part 4 that relate to entitlement (sections 77(3), 77(4), 83, 84, 88(1))
-- are combined with the section's own result by this conjunction: any "no" makes a "no", all "yes" makes a "yes", and
-- anything else is NOTHING. Used by sections 78(6) and 79(6).
-- src:1368 | (6) This section is subject to the provisions of this Part, or regulations under it, relating to entitlement to the daily living component (see in particular sections 82 (persons who are terminally ill) and 83 (persons of pensionable age)).
@ref s 78(6) (src:1368)
GIVEN `the results` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a result is JUST FALSE, which the caller took from its own quoted "if", "unless", "while" or flat negative
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) `the results` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a result is not covered, and no result is a "no"
        IF elem NOTHING `the results` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Sections 78(6) and 79(6) speak of "the provisions of this Part ... relating to entitlement" the section is subject to. The
-- section's own result is the standard rate under (1) OR the enhanced rate under (2) (or, for the daily living component,
-- section 82(2)): a "yes" in either gives a "yes", a "no" in every one gives a "no", and anything else is NOTHING.
-- src:1368 | (6) This section is subject to the provisions of this Part, or regulations under it, relating to entitlement to the daily living component (see in particular sections 82 (persons who are terminally ill) and 83 (persons of pensionable age)).
@ref s 78(6) own result (src:1368)
GIVEN `the results` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(6) the disjunction of the results` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) `the results` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no result is a "yes" and a result is not covered
        IF elem NOTHING `the results` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): every result is JUST FALSE, each taken from its own quoted "if", "unless", "while" or flat negative
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- (1) standard rate: ability limited AND the required period condition met. (2) enhanced rate: severely limited AND met.
-- "limited" and "severely limited" are decided in accordance with regulations (section 80(1)), so each is an input.
-- src:1355 | (1) A person is entitled to the daily living component at the standard rate if—
-- src:1356 | (a) the person's ability to carry out daily living activities is limited by the person's physical or mental condition; and
-- src:1357 | (b) the person meets the required period condition.
@ref s 78(1) (src:1355-1357)
GIVEN `the person's ability to carry out daily living activities is limited by the person's physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person meets the required period condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(1) the person is entitled to the daily living component at the standard rate` MEANS
    IF `the person's ability to carry out daily living activities is limited by the person's physical or mental condition`
    THEN CONSIDER `the person meets the required period condition`
         WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to the daily living component at the standard rate if ... (b) the person meets the required period condition" failed (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the required period condition has not been determined
         WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to the daily living component at the standard rate if (a) the person's ability to carry out daily living activities is limited" failed (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1358 | (2) A person is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate if—
-- src:1359 | (a) the person's ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition; and
-- src:1360 | (b) the person meets the required period condition.
@ref s 78(2) (src:1358-1360)
GIVEN `the person's ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person meets the required period condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(2) the person is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate` MEANS
    IF `the person's ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition`
    THEN CONSIDER `the person meets the required period condition`
         WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate if ... (b) the person meets the required period condition" failed (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the required period condition has not been determined
         WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate if (a) the person's ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited" failed (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (3) the weekly rates are "such weekly rate as may be prescribed": the regulations are not among the sources.
-- src:1361 | (3) In this section, in relation to the daily living component—
-- src:1362 | (a) “the standard rate” means such weekly rate as may be prescribed;
-- src:1363 | (b) “the enhanced rate” means such weekly rate as may be prescribed.
@ref s 78(3) (src:1361-1363)
GIVEN `the standard weekly rate regulations prescribe for the daily living component` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78(3)(a) the weekly rate of the daily living component at the standard rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the standard weekly rate regulations prescribe for the daily living component`
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST n
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such weekly rate as may be prescribed"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the enhanced weekly rate regulations prescribe for the daily living component` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78(3)(b) the weekly rate of the daily living component at the enhanced rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the enhanced weekly rate regulations prescribe for the daily living component`
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST n
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such weekly rate as may be prescribed"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the rate` IS A `Rate of a component`
      `the standard weekly rate regulations prescribe for the daily living component` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the enhanced weekly rate regulations prescribe for the daily living component` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78(3) the weekly rate of the daily living component at the rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rate`
    WHEN `standard rate` THEN `s 78(3)(a) the weekly rate of the daily living component at the standard rate` `the standard weekly rate regulations prescribe for the daily living component`
    WHEN `enhanced rate` THEN `s 78(3)(b) the weekly rate of the daily living component at the enhanced rate` `the enhanced weekly rate regulations prescribe for the daily living component`

-- (4) "daily living activities" means such activities as may be prescribed for the purposes of this section.
-- src:1364 | (4) In this Part “daily living activities“ means such activities as may be prescribed for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 78(4) (src:1364)
GIVEN `the activity` IS A STRING
      `the activities regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 78` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(4) the activity is a daily living activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the activities regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 78`
    WHEN JUST activities THEN
        IF elem `the activity` activities
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“daily living activities“ means such activities as may be prescribed" (a closed definition, once the prescribed activities are supplied)
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the activities are left to regulations
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (6) "This section is subject to the provisions of this Part, or regulations under it, relating to entitlement to the
-- daily living component (see in particular sections 82 and 83)": the result under (1) or (2) (or section 82(2)) is
-- combined with the results of the other provisions, which the caller supplies.
-- src:1368 | (6) This section is subject to the provisions of this Part, or regulations under it, relating to entitlement to the daily living component (see in particular sections 82 (persons who are terminally ill) and 83 (persons of pensionable age)).
@ref s 78(6) (src:1368)
GIVEN `the person's own result under section 78(1) or (2), or section 82(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the results of the other provisions of Part 4 relating to entitlement to the daily living component` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(6) the person is entitled to the daily living component, subject to the other provisions of Part 4 relating to entitlement` MEANS
    `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` (`the person's own result under section 78(1) or (2), or section 82(2)` FOLLOWED BY `the results of the other provisions of Part 4 relating to entitlement to the daily living component`)

§ `s 79 Mobility component`

-- (1)(a) and (2)(a): "of or over the age prescribed for the purposes of this subsection"; each subsection has its own
-- prescription, so each has its own input.
-- src:1370 | (1) A person is entitled to the mobility component at the standard rate if—
-- src:1371 | (a) the person is of or over the age prescribed for the purposes of this subsection;
-- src:1372 | (b) the person's ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by the person's physical or mental condition; and
-- src:1373 | (c) the person meets the required period condition.
@ref s 79(1) (src:1370-1373)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
      `the age regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 79(1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(1)(a) the person is of or over the age prescribed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the age regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 79(1)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person is of or over the age prescribed" is a limb of an "if" and a person under that age fails it (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the person`'s `age in years` AT LEAST n)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the age prescribed for the purposes of this subsection" is left to regulations
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the person's ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by the person's physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is of or over the age prescribed for the purposes of section 79(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person meets the required period condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(1) the person is entitled to the mobility component at the standard rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to the mobility component at the standard rate if ... (b) the person's ability to carry out mobility activities is limited" failed (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
        IF NOT `the person's ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by the person's physical or mental condition` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- the age limb (a) and the required period limb (c): a "no" from either is a "no", a not-covered from either is not covered
        OTHERWISE `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` (LIST `the person is of or over the age prescribed for the purposes of section 79(1)`, `the person meets the required period condition`)

-- src:1374 | (2) A person is entitled to the mobility component at the enhanced rate if—
-- src:1375 | (a) the person is of or over the age prescribed for the purposes of this subsection;
-- src:1376 | (b) the person's ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition; and
-- src:1377 | (c) the person meets the required period condition.
@ref s 79(2) (src:1374-1377)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
      `the age regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 79(2)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(2)(a) the person is of or over the age prescribed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the age regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 79(2)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person is of or over the age prescribed" is a limb of an "if" and a person under that age fails it (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the person`'s `age in years` AT LEAST n)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the age prescribed for the purposes of this subsection" is left to regulations
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the person's ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is of or over the age prescribed for the purposes of section 79(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person meets the required period condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(2) the person is entitled to the mobility component at the enhanced rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to the mobility component at the enhanced rate if ... (b) the person's ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited" failed (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
        IF NOT `the person's ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` (LIST `the person is of or over the age prescribed for the purposes of section 79(2)`, `the person meets the required period condition`)

-- src:1378 | (3) In this section, in relation to the mobility component—
-- src:1379 | (a) “the standard rate” means such weekly rate as may be prescribed;
-- src:1380 | (b) “the enhanced rate” means such weekly rate as may be prescribed.
@ref s 79(3) (src:1378-1380)
GIVEN `the standard weekly rate regulations prescribe for the mobility component` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 79(3)(a) the weekly rate of the mobility component at the standard rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the standard weekly rate regulations prescribe for the mobility component`
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST n
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such weekly rate as may be prescribed"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the enhanced weekly rate regulations prescribe for the mobility component` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 79(3)(b) the weekly rate of the mobility component at the enhanced rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the enhanced weekly rate regulations prescribe for the mobility component`
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST n
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such weekly rate as may be prescribed"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the rate` IS A `Rate of a component`
      `the standard weekly rate regulations prescribe for the mobility component` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the enhanced weekly rate regulations prescribe for the mobility component` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 79(3) the weekly rate of the mobility component at the rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rate`
    WHEN `standard rate` THEN `s 79(3)(a) the weekly rate of the mobility component at the standard rate` `the standard weekly rate regulations prescribe for the mobility component`
    WHEN `enhanced rate` THEN `s 79(3)(b) the weekly rate of the mobility component at the enhanced rate` `the enhanced weekly rate regulations prescribe for the mobility component`

-- src:1381 | (4) In this Part “mobility activities” means such activities as may be prescribed for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 79(4) (src:1381)
GIVEN `the activity` IS A STRING
      `the activities regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 79` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(4) the activity is a mobility activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the activities regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 79`
    WHEN JUST activities THEN
        IF elem `the activity` activities
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“mobility activities” means such activities as may be prescribed" (a closed definition, once the prescribed activities are supplied)
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the activities are left to regulations
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (7) Regulations may provide that a person is not entitled to the mobility component for a period in prescribed
-- circumstances where the person is unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility. The input says whether regulations so
-- provide for this person and period.
-- src:1386 | (7) Regulations may provide that a person is not entitled to the mobility component for a period (even though the requirements in subsection (1) or (2) are met) in prescribed circumstances where the person's condition is such that during all or most of the period the person is unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility.
@ref s 79(7) (src:1386)
GIVEN `regulations provide that the person is not entitled to the mobility component for the period because the person is unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(7) the person is not barred by regulations about unlikelihood of benefiting from enhanced mobility` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations provide that the person is not entitled to the mobility component for the period because the person is unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Regulations may provide that a person is not entitled to the mobility component for a period (even though the requirements in subsection (1) or (2) are met)" and the regulations so provide (a lawyer's reading (b): the "no" rests on the regulations' say-so)
    WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations so provide is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

-- src:1385 | (6) This section is subject to the provisions of this Part, or regulations under it, relating to entitlement to the mobility component (see in particular sections 82 and 83).
@ref s 79(6) (src:1385)
GIVEN `the person's own result under section 79(1) or (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the results of the other provisions of Part 4 relating to entitlement to the mobility component` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(6) the person is entitled to the mobility component, subject to the other provisions of Part 4 relating to entitlement` MEANS
    `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` (`the person's own result under section 79(1) or (2)` FOLLOWED BY `the results of the other provisions of Part 4 relating to entitlement to the mobility component`)

§ `s 80 Ability to carry out daily living activities or mobility activities`

-- (1) The four questions, "to be determined in accordance with regulations". The determinations made under the regulations
-- are inputs.
-- src:1388 | (1) For the purposes of this Part, the following questions are to be determined in accordance with regulations—
-- src:1389 | (a) whether a person's ability to carry out daily living activities is limited by the person's physical or mental condition;
-- src:1390 | (b) whether a person's ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition;
-- src:1391 | (c) whether a person's ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by the person's physical or mental condition;
-- src:1392 | (d) whether a person's ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition.
@ref s 80(1) (src:1388-1392)
DECLARE `s 80(1) question about the person's ability` IS ONE OF
    `s 80(1)(a) daily living activities limited`
    `s 80(1)(b) daily living activities severely limited`
    `s 80(1)(c) mobility activities limited`
    `s 80(1)(d) mobility activities severely limited`

DECLARE `s 80(1) determinations made in accordance with regulations` HAS
    `the answer to question (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer to question (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer to question (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer to question (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref s 80(1) (src:1388-1392)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `s 80(1) question about the person's ability`
      `the determinations` IS A `s 80(1) determinations made in accordance with regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(1) the question as determined in accordance with regulations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the question`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): each answer is "determined in accordance with regulations"; NOTHING when no determination is supplied
    WHEN `s 80(1)(a) daily living activities limited`          THEN `the determinations`'s `the answer to question (a)`
    WHEN `s 80(1)(b) daily living activities severely limited` THEN `the determinations`'s `the answer to question (b)`
    WHEN `s 80(1)(c) mobility activities limited`              THEN `the determinations`'s `the answer to question (c)`
    WHEN `s 80(1)(d) mobility activities severely limited`     THEN `the determinations`'s `the answer to question (d)`

-- (4)(c) and (5)(a): the regulations may require a person to take part in a consultation, and may provide for a negative
-- determination to be treated as made if a person fails without a good reason to comply with that requirement.
-- src:1402 | (5) The regulations may include provision—
-- src:1403 | (a) for a negative determination to be treated as made if a person fails without a good reason to comply with a requirement imposed under subsection (4);
@ref s 80(5)(a) (src:1402-1403)
GIVEN `regulations provide that a negative determination is treated as made if a person fails without a good reason to comply with a requirement imposed under section 80(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with a requirement imposed under section 80(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a good reason for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(5)(a) a negative determination is treated as made against the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations provide that a negative determination is treated as made if a person fails without a good reason to comply with a requirement imposed under section 80(4)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person fails to comply with a requirement imposed under section 80(4)` AND (NOT `the person has a good reason for the failure`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision reaches only a person who "fails without a good reason to comply"; the text is silent on anyone else
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): regulations "may include" the provision; if they do not, the text says nothing
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations so provide is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

-- (6) "negative determination" means a determination that a person does not meet the requirements of section 78(1)(a) and (b)
-- or (2)(a) and (b) (daily living component), or section 79(1)(a) to (c) or (2)(a) to (c) (mobility component).
-- src:1406 | (6) In subsection (5)(a) a “negative determination” means a determination that a person does not meet the requirements of—
-- src:1407 | (a) section 78(1)(a) and (b) or (2)(a) and (b) (daily living component);
-- src:1408 | (b) section 79(1)(a) to (c) or (2)(a) to (c) (mobility component).
@ref s 80(6) (src:1406-1408)
DECLARE `s 80(6) determination about the requirements for a component` IS ONE OF
    `s 80(6)(a) a finding that the person does not meet the requirements of section 78(1)(a) and (b) or (2)(a) and (b)`
    `s 80(6)(b) a finding that the person does not meet the requirements of section 79(1)(a) to (c) or (2)(a) to (c)`
    `s 80(6) any other determination`

@ref s 80(6) (src:1406-1408)
GIVEN `the determination` IS A `s 80(6) determination about the requirements for a component`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(6) the determination is a negative determination` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the determination`
    WHEN `s 80(6)(a) a finding that the person does not meet the requirements of section 78(1)(a) and (b) or (2)(a) and (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 80(6)(b) a finding that the person does not meet the requirements of section 79(1)(a) to (c) or (2)(a) to (c)`   THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “negative determination” means a determination that a person does not meet the requirements of" (a closed definition)
    WHEN `s 80(6) any other determination` THEN JUST FALSE

