-- (3)(b) "the previous 3 months" means the 3 months ending with the prescribed date; (3)(c) "the next 9 months" means the
-- 9 months beginning with the day after that date. A month is counted as a calendar month, from the corresponding date;
-- see the fork register (F-81-2) for the month-end reading taken.
-- src:1416 | (3) In subsection (1)—
-- src:1417 | (a) “assessed” means assessed in accordance with regulations under section 80;
-- src:1418 | (b) “the previous 3 months” means the 3 months ending with the prescribed date;
-- src:1419 | (c) “the next 9 months” means the 9 months beginning with the day after that date.
@ref s 81(3) (src:1416-1419)
GIVEN `the prescribed date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`s 81(3)(b) the previous 3 months ending with the prescribed date` MEANS
    Period WITH
        `first day` IS `add months` (`the prescribed date` PLUS 1) (0 MINUS 3)
        `last day`  IS `the prescribed date`

-- A period of months that begins on a given day ends on the day before the corresponding date that many months on; when
-- the later month has no such date, it ends on that month's last day (the calendar-month reading, fork F-81-2).
@ref s 81(3) (src:1418-1419)
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 81(3) the last day of the months beginning with the day` MEANS
    LET `the corresponding date` MEANS `add months` `the first day` `the number of months`
    IN IF DATE_DAY `the corresponding date` EQUALS DATE_DAY `the first day`
       THEN `the corresponding date` MINUS 1
       ELSE `the corresponding date`

@ref s 81(3)(c) (src:1419)
GIVEN `the prescribed date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`s 81(3)(c) the next 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` MEANS
    Period WITH
        `first day` IS `the prescribed date` PLUS 1
        `last day`  IS `s 81(3) the last day of the months beginning with the day` (`the prescribed date` PLUS 1) 9

@ref s 81(1)(a), s 81(3)(b) (src:1418)
GIVEN `the time` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1)(a) the time is within the previous 3 months` MEANS
    LET `the months` MEANS `s 81(3)(b) the previous 3 months ending with the prescribed date` `the prescribed date`
    IN `the time` AT LEAST `the months`'s `first day` AND `the time` AT MOST `the months`'s `last day`

@ref s 81(1)(b), s 81(3)(c) (src:1419)
GIVEN `the time` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1)(b) the time is within the next 9 months` MEANS
    LET `the months` MEANS `s 81(3)(c) the next 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` `the prescribed date`
    IN `the time` AT LEAST `the months`'s `first day` AND `the time` AT MOST `the months`'s `last day`

-- (1) Regulations under section 80(2) "must provide for the question of whether a person meets 'the required period
-- condition' ... to be determined by reference to (a) ... and (b) ...". Read here as the usual test: the condition is met
-- when both limbs hold and not met when either fails (fork F-81-1; a lawyer's reading, listed under Marginal readings).
-- src:1410 | (1) Regulations under section 80(2) must provide for the question of whether a person meets “the required period condition” for the purposes of section 78(1) or (2) or 79(1) or (2) to be determined by reference to—
-- src:1411 | (a) whether, as respects every time in the previous 3 months, it is likely that if the relevant ability had been assessed at that time that ability would have been determined to be limited or (as the case may be) severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition; and
-- src:1412 | (b) whether, as respects every time in the next 9 months, it is likely that if the relevant ability were to be assessed at that time that ability would be determined to be limited or (as the case may be) severely limited by the person's physical or mental condition.
@ref s 81(1) (src:1410-1412)
GIVEN `as respects every time in the previous 3 months, it is likely that if the relevant ability had been assessed at that time it would have been determined to be limited or severely limited, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as respects every time in the next 9 months, it is likely that if the relevant ability were to be assessed at that time it would be determined to be limited or severely limited, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) the person meets the required period condition on the usual test` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `as respects every time in the previous 3 months, it is likely that if the relevant ability had been assessed at that time it would have been determined to be limited or severely limited, as the case may be`
           AND `as respects every time in the next 9 months, it is likely that if the relevant ability were to be assessed at that time it would be determined to be limited or severely limited, as the case may be`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "determined by reference to (a) whether ... and (b) whether ..." a limb fails (a lawyer's reading: the limbs are read as the test, fork F-81-1)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- (4) Regulations may provide that in prescribed cases the question is not determined under subsections (1) to (3) but
-- as the regulations provide for those cases.
-- src:1420 | (4) Regulations under section 80(2) may provide that in prescribed cases the question of whether a person meets “the required period condition” for the purposes of section 78(1) or (2) or 79(1) or (2)—
-- src:1421 | (a) is not to be determined in accordance with the provision made by virtue of subsections (1) to (3) above;
-- src:1422 | (b) is to be determined in accordance with provision made in relation to those cases by the regulations.
@ref s 81(4) (src:1420-1422)
GIVEN `regulations provide that in the person's case the question is determined otherwise than under section 81(1) to (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result on the usual test` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result under the regulations' provision for that case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(4) the person meets the required period condition` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations provide that in the person's case the question is determined otherwise than under section 81(1) to (3)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN `the result under the regulations' provision for that case`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `the result on the usual test`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person's case is a prescribed case is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

§ `s 82 Terminal illness`

-- (4) "terminally ill" at any time: the person suffers from a progressive disease and the person's death in consequence of
-- that disease can reasonably be expected within 12 months. The 12 months are the 12 months beginning with the time; the
-- last day is the day before the corresponding date a year on (fork F-82).
-- src:1430 | (4) For the purposes of this section a person is “terminally ill” at any time if at that time the person suffers from a progressive disease and the person's death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 12 months.
@ref s 82(4) (src:1430)
GIVEN `the time` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 82(4) the last day of the 12 months beginning with the time` MEANS
    `s 81(3) the last day of the months beginning with the day` `the time` 12

GIVEN `the person suffers from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time` IS A DATE
      `the date by which the person's death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(4) the person is terminally ill at the time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person suffers from a progressive disease`
           AND `the date by which the person's death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` AT MOST `s 82(4) the last day of the 12 months beginning with the time` `the time`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is “terminally ill” at any time if at that time the person suffers from a progressive disease and the person's death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 12 months" (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- (1) This section applies to a person who (a) is terminally ill and (b) has made a claim for personal independence
-- payment expressly on the ground of terminal illness.
-- src:1425 | (1) This section applies to a person who—
-- src:1426 | (a) is terminally ill; and
-- src:1427 | (b) has made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground of terminal illness.
@ref s 82(1) (src:1425-1427)
GIVEN `the person is terminally ill` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground of terminal illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(1) this section applies to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is terminally ill`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person has made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground of terminal illness`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section "applies to a person who ... has made a claim ... expressly on the ground of terminal illness"; the text is silent on anyone else
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section "applies to a person who is terminally ill"; the text is silent on anyone else
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the person is terminally ill has not been determined
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

