    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "a person to whom this section applies"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

@ref s 82(2) (src:1428)
GIVEN `section 82 applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(2) section 78(1) and (2) apply to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `section 82 applies to the person`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "accordingly section 78(1) and (2) do not apply to such a person"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "such a person", a person to whom the section applies
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

-- The person's own result for the daily living component: section 82(2) where it applies, otherwise section 78(1) or (2).
@ref s 82(2) (src:1428)
GIVEN `section 82 applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result under section 78(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
