    CONSIDER `s 82(2) the person is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate` `section 82 applies to the person`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 82(2) says nothing where the section does not apply, so the result under section 78(2) stands
    OTHERWISE `the result under section 78(2)`

-- The result under section 78(1) for a person to whom section 82 applies: "accordingly section 78(1) and (2) do not apply to
-- such a person", so the person is not entitled under section 78(1) (the entitlement is section 82(2)'s, at the enhanced rate).
-- For anyone else the result under section 78(1) stands.
