    CONSIDER `s 82(2) section 78(1) and (2) apply to the person` `section 82 applies to the person`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "accordingly section 78(1) and (2) do not apply to such a person"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "such a person", a person to whom the section applies; for anyone else the result under section 78(1) stands
    OTHERWISE `the result under section 78(1)`

-- (3) Section 79(1)(c) and (2)(c) (the required period condition for the mobility component) do not apply to a person to
