    CONSIDER `section 82 applies to the person`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 79(1)(c) and (2)(c) (required period condition for mobility component) do not apply to a person to whom this section applies"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "a person to whom this section applies"
