    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

-- The mobility component's required period condition limb, as it stands for the person: where section 82 applies, limbs
-- 79(1)(c) and (2)(c) "do not apply", so the limb is not one the person can fail and counts as satisfied; where it does not
-- apply (or that is not known) the limb is the caller's result.
-- src:1429 | (3) Section 79(1)(c) and (2)(c) (required period condition for mobility component) do not apply to a person to whom this section applies.
@ref s 82(3) the limb as it stands (src:1429)
GIVEN `section 82 applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person meets the required period condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(3) the required period condition limb of section 79(1)(c) and (2)(c), as it stands for the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 82(3) the required period condition of section 79(1)(c) and (2)(c) applies to the person` `section 82 applies to the person`
    -- the limb does not apply to the person, so it cannot be failed: it counts as satisfied
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 82(3) is about "a person to whom this section applies"; for anyone else the limb stands as the caller's result
    OTHERWISE `the person meets the required period condition`

-- (5) A claim made on behalf of another, expressly on the ground that the other is terminally ill, is regarded as the
-- other's own claim, despite its being made without that person's knowledge or authority.
-- src:1431 | (5) For the purposes of this section, where—
-- src:1432 | (a) a person purports to make a claim for personal independence payment on behalf of another, and
-- src:1433 | (b) the claim is made expressly on the ground that the person on whose behalf it purports to be made is terminally ill,
-- src:1434 | that person is to be regarded as making the claim despite its being made without that person's knowledge or authority.
@ref s 82(5) (src:1431-1434)
GIVEN `a person purports to make a claim for personal independence payment on behalf of another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made expressly on the ground that the person on whose behalf it purports to be made is terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made without that person's knowledge or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(5) the person on whose behalf the claim purports to be made is regarded as making the claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- the knowledge or authority of the person does not matter: "despite its being made without that person's knowledge or authority"
        IF `a person purports to make a claim for personal independence payment on behalf of another`
           AND `the claim is made expressly on the ground that the person on whose behalf it purports to be made is terminally ill`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for a claim made on behalf of another "expressly on the ground" of terminal illness
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

