-- src:1443 | (1) A person to whom a relevant EU Regulation applies is not entitled to the daily living component for a period unless during that period the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Title III of the Regulation in question.
@ref s 84(1) (src:1443)
GIVEN `a relevant EU Regulation applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `during the period the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Title III of the Regulation in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) the person is not barred from the daily living component by the United Kingdom not being the competent state` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a relevant EU Regulation applies to the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `during the period the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Title III of the Regulation in question` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person to whom a relevant EU Regulation applies is not entitled to the daily living component for a period unless during that period the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
